UniXNU (github.com/Droid-VM/UniXNU) 2e61915, drivers/NativeRamBlock, BSD-2-Clause-Patent (LICENSE). Vendored 2026-11-11 so the
native build reads no driver source from outside this repository.

UniXNU-piano changes (NativeRamBlock.cpp), formerly applied at build time by tooling/k27/build-native-ram-block.sh:
- publishWhenBSDMatched (the change macOS-DroidVM's scripts/build-native-ram-block.py applied): the disk is published from a
  thread once IOResources has matched IOBSD (APFS deadlocks otherwise); then it waits for NativeUfs's root layout
  (native_ufs_store_ready), opens the store and only then publishes the disk.
- The six native_ufs_store_* hooks are plain imports (the KC linker takes no weak imports): NativeUfs provides them (data-persist=2).
  The upstream virtio data store is not part of the native build.
- attachStore logs "NativeRamBlock: Data store state ...".

UniXNU-piano changes of 2026-11-11 (docs/data-store.md):
- The store guard (PersistOverlay.h open -> Open::Kept, state 7): a valid store made for another seed is left untouched and the disk
  runs volatile for that boot, unless data-store-replace=1 (or =0x<the store's 8 hex>) or sheng-data-reset=1|2 asks to start over.
  Upstream re-initialised it ("stale"), which dropped every Data change whenever a RAM image brought another seed.
- VolatileDisk.h: a large seed (above 2 GiB) without the store open read-write has a volatile write path (pages in RAM); upstream
  refused its writes (kIOReturnNotReady). The read-only probe (data-persist=1) of a large disk no longer dereferences sparse.pages.
- Self-contained stores (header extension "SHNGEXT1" in bytes 64..127 of block 0, flag kSelfContained) and Overlay::flatten
  (data-store-flatten=1): every seed page written into the store, then the flag; DirectDisk.h then reads clear bits as zero, so the
  store works with any seed of its size. The version 1 header (bytes 0..63) is unchanged, so earlier kernels still read the store.
- Test/: upstream's host tests sparse.cpp, persist.cpp (its stale-seed case now expects Kept, then Fresh with replace), direct.cpp,
  seeddisk.cpp, seed-identity.cpp (sparse.cpp: the over-size case moved past SparseDisk.h's 1 TiB limit); new guard.cpp and
  volatile.cpp; run-tests.sh.
- native-ram-trace=1 (2026-11-11, docs/forensics-2026-11-11.md): a console line before and after each step of the store's set-up
  (the waits for IOBSD and NativeUfs's root layout, the GPT check, the window, the header and bitmap I/O, the syncs, the disk's
  registration), with the milliseconds since the publish thread started. Off without the argument; the set-up's I/O is unchanged.
